<p>I like this idea, but the test logs are already summarized in the description (i think) before you even read them. Perhaps the tests would benefit from examining the effects of some memories that aren't only good? Maybe its just not the intended tone of the skip, but what if someone was told to remember an exposure to a cognitohazard or some sort of SCP that manifests physical symptoms upon visual contact. Do those symptoms only exist in the mental world? Just a spicy suggestion.</p>

